WEBVTT

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.030
Hina-chan!

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:19.520
Welcome home, Hina-chan! Perfect timing!

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:23.280
I wanted to ask you a little favor.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:28.540
You see, the wind yesterday knocked down 
our scarecrow and broke it.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:33.190
And, you know, animals have 
always liked you, right?

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:35.970
I know it sounds funny to ask you 
to take a scarecrow's place,

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.720
but if you'd stick around near the field

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:42.020
and attract the animals to you, 
it'd be a great help.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.750
It's this way...

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:45.930
Oh, my!

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:50.440
I guess I startled you when I just 
showed up and started talking to you.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.190
There you go.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.890
All you have to do is stay right here.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:57.440
Thank you so much.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.260
Take a scarecrow's place?

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:05.170
Oh, Hina-chan's taking the scarecrow's place?

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:05.700
Yep.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:10.980
All the animals go straight 
to her. It's a big help!

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:14.980
She's much more reliable 
than any real scarecrow.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:16.710
She sure is.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:23.810
Hina-chan, thank you for 
being our scarecrow today.

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.100
Thanks a bunch.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:28.100
You're such a sweet girl.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:33.100
I wish we had a scarecrow 
as cute as you in our fields.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.730
It's not often we see 
such a quiet girl, is it?

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:41.110
She never says a word. Just like a doll!

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:43.630
She really is just like a scarecrow.

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:45.390
She has the spirit of a pro!

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.370
This is just the way I've always been...

00:03:57.230 --> 00:04:01.120
Standing in the field 
every day is exhausting.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:04.000
There's nothing to do out here...

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.810
But I can't just tell them 
I'm quitting now...

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:10.140
Thanks for always helping out.

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:14.740
Thanks to you, the animals 
don't come close anymore,

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:18.180
so we can concentrate on working 
in the fields without worrying.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:21.400
Take these to eat with your family.

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:26.580
Th-Th-Than...

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:27.350
Than?

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:28.660
Than...

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:32.000
Mom, I'm home.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.420
Oh, Hinako. Welcome back.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.120
You were out late again, huh?

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.890
Here, use these for dinner tonight.

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:41.420
Oh, thank you...

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:48.950
<i>Lately, Hinako's been bringing 
vegetables from somewhere.</i>

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:50.930
<i>And she's been getting home late.</i>

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:54.940
<i>Sh-She couldn't be stealing 
from the fields, could she?!</i>

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.370
<i>No, no! That can't be it!</i>

00:04:57.370 --> 00:04:59.350
<i>I trust my little girl!</i>

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:04.950
<i>I'm sleepy...</i>

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:08.610
<i>It's so warm out today.</i>

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:11.580
<i>It's making me sleepy.</i>

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.740
Oh, it's Hina-chan.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:14.580
Oh!

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:17.610
She's here to be our scarecrow again today?

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:19.080
What a big help she is!

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:23.320
Oh, right. I'll get her vegetables for today.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:26.090
She'll catch a cold 
if she stays out here like this.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:33.090
Wow! There are so many!

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:35.480
H-Huh? What is this?

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:38.850
Am I a jizo statue now? 
When did this happen?

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:42.130
Oh!

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:44.610
Hey, Hina-chan!

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.400
Thanks for being our scarecrow again today.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.110
You were a big help.

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:55.760
U-Um... These... I... I should 
also... tha... than...

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:59.450
Hurry on home before it gets dark.

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:01.170
Come by again, okay?

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:07.910
Wow!

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:11.330
This is great, Hinako! 
Thanks for always bringing these!

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:18.820
I know. I still haven't been able 
to thank them for the vegetables.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:20.910
What should I do?

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:25.210
Yeah, you're right. All I can do is practice.

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:26.530
I'll try my best.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:31.950
<b>Hina Mama</b>

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:31.950
<b>My daughter is currently wearing 
a costume and talking to a bird...</b>

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:53.470
Tanuki-san, you can be the old man, okay?

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:57.000
He and his wife are always very kind to me,

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.460
so I want to be able to thank them properly.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:01.110
Help me out, okay?

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:03.560
Here I go. Let's see...

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:07.070
"Hey, Hina-chan! 
Working hard again today, eh?"

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.570
"Hello, sir. Thank you 
for all you've done for me."

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:13.380
"Here are your vegetables for today."

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:14.580
"Eat them all up."

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:19.710
"Thank you very much, sir. 
I always enjoy your vegetables."

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:20.960
"Is that right?"

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:24.010
"Yes. My mother always 
looks forward to them, too.

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:27.300
Recently, when she sees the 
vegetables I bring home,

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.720
she starts planning our meals 
for the week with them."

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.220
"Oh?"

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:35.470
"The vegetables from your fields
 are so delicious!"

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:39.090
There! I practiced! 
I said everything perfectly!

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:39.900
Hina-chan.

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:40.850
Y-Yes?!

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:44.270
You did great work again today. Thank you.

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:45.730
Here, take this.

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:50.610
U-Uh...

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.960
See you again tomorrow, okay?

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:55.700
The vegetables...

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:59.920
The vegetables... are delicious.

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:03.000
Th-Thank you for always giving them to me.

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:06.500
I should be thanking you. 
I'll be counting on you again, I'm sure.

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:10.610
Y-Yesh! I'll try my besht!

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:13.560
Better try your best to get better 
at speaking, too, eh?

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.580
I'm...

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:35.360
That's right. I'm in Tokyo now.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:37.910
I have to try my hardest here.

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:40.960
I have to try hard so I can stand on a stage

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:43.700
and learn to talk skillfully to people.

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:46.170
Oh, yeah...

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:51.170
<b>It Begins Here</b>

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:50.410
The high school's 
theater club is on hiatus...

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.810
Morning, Hina-chan!

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:03.770
Oh, good morning.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:04.770
Morning.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:07.570
Oh, Miss Landlady. Good morning.

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:09.130
Good morning.

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:13.190
Oh, Kuu-chan's here, too. 
I'll get breakfast ready right away.

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:18.820
Go on. Eat up.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:20.450
Let's eat!

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:26.340
What do you think, Hina-chan?

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:28.460
It's really delicious!

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:32.900
By the way, are you really going to 
start a theater troupe, Hina-chan?

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:33.340
Huh?

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:38.450
Um, Miss Landlady...

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:39.560
Yes?

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:46.110
The theater club is on hiatus because 
the advisor left on a theater trip, right?

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:47.850
Yeah, that's right.

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:50.800
Why did the advisor leave, though?

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:51.980
Because...

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:57.790
Sensei, why?!

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:01.740
As I am now, I'm not fit to be your advisor.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:05.560
I'll come back when I am!

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:11.700
She said she suddenly felt that 
her skills had reached a limit.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:15.260
Sh-She sounds like a passionate teacher.

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:18.710
What are the other members of the club doing?

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:21.920
They're all keeping active in their own ways,

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:24.730
going out for TV auditions and such.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:29.300
But you've just been practicing by yourself 
at the park all this time, right?

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:34.270
I want to act with everyone.

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:36.530
Miss Landlady...

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:40.520
<i>She really loves acting.</i>

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:42.030
Hina-chan.

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:45.660
Why do you want to get into theater?

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:49.180
U-Um... I...

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:52.170
Are you already an actress?

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.920
Is there any role 
you're particularly good at?

00:10:55.890 --> 00:10:58.040
Obviously, that would be a scarecrow.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:04.930
<b>Cue Card</b>

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:07.430
<b>Coffee Shop Hitotose</b>

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:11.650
So that's why you want to be in theater.

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:12.850
Yes.

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:17.170
As you can see, I get so nervous 
in front of people, and I want to fix that.

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:19.440
That's why I want to try theater.

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:24.950
B-But I'm never going to get 
anywhere this way, am I?

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:29.140
Don't worry. I was nervous 
at my first performance, too.

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:31.400
I couldn't say my lines very well.

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:33.080
R-Really?

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:36.370
Yeah. I was four years old.

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:37.960
F-Four?!

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:41.370
That's right, you were a 
child actress, weren't you?

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:45.050
My dad was a stage actor,

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:48.520
so it happened naturally while 
I helped at his rehearsals.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:49.710
Chiaki-chan.

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:50.230
Yes?

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:52.490
Can you grab those props for me?

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:53.690
Okay.

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:58.730
We've got trouble! The girl 
playing Girl A suddenly got sick!

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:02.120
Oh, no! Will we have to cancel today's show?

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:04.110
Wait, I know!

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:07.470
Chiaki-chan, can you be a stand-in?

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:08.620
Huh?

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:13.200
Uh... um...

00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:15.850
That's what happened.

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:19.630
That would make anyone nervous, child or not!

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:22.600
Is your father still a stage actor?

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:24.440
You're so cute! Is that food yummy?

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:27.160
No, my dad became a guitarist after that.

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:25.990
Oh, really?

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:32.270
He travels the world, playing and singing, 
while he manages an apartment building.

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:36.310
Right now, he's apparently 
playing the maracas.

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:42.520
Sounds like quite a free spirit...

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:48.030
<b>1) Slice the apple into rings. 
Leave the peel on!
2) Coat the inside of a pie pan with butter. 
Lay the thawed crust in the pan and trim any excess. 
Poke a few holes in the bottom with
 a fork and chill in the refrigerator for 30 minutes.
Use a cookie cutter for cute and easy core removal!
Let the slices sit in salt water. Don't forget to peel them!!
Butter the pie crust!
30 minutes!</b>

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:48.030
<b>Cooking Drill: Apple Pie 
Ingredients 
1 frozen pie crust 
1 apple 
30g sugar 
1/2 tbsp. lemon juice 
Small amount of butter 
*Thaw the pie crust at room temperature.</b>

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:06.300
Oh, it sounds like it's going to rain soon.

00:13:06.770 --> 00:13:09.140
Huh? But it's so sunny.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.430
Aw, man...

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:13.560
And I thought we'd be able 
to dry the laundry...

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:19.240
Hina-chan, can you talk to animals?

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:23.150
Oh, no, um... 
It's more like just intuition...

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:24.440
Wow!

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:27.650
Animals have always been drawn to me.

00:13:27.650 --> 00:13:31.680
Like rabbits, tanuki, boars, deer...

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:33.950
After a while, it just came naturally.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:38.420
<i>I think she'd be more suited to 
the circus than to theater...</i>

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:39.960
Is something wrong?

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:46.830
Hina-chan, why don't we try 
forming a theater troupe after all?

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:47.440
Huh?

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:52.970
What you said earlier made me see 
that you really want to be in theater.

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:58.770
But there's no telling when the school 
theater club will start up again.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:13:59.960
B-But...

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:01.240
Let's do it!

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:01.980
Kuu-chan...

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:07.740
How about we make use of your talent 
to put on a play with real animals?

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:11.060
Like <i>The Three Little Pigs</i>.

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:15.520
But that story wouldn't need 
any human actors, would it?

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:17.750
That's true... Okay, then...

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:19.580
Maybe <i>Little Red Riding Hood</i>?

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:22.050
Whoever played the grandma would be killed!

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:24.370
She'd get eaten by the wolf!

00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:27.300
Actually, didn't Little Red 
Riding Hood get eaten, too?

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.010
We can't do that!

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:31.060
This is harder than I thought.

00:14:31.060 --> 00:14:33.050
Um, Miss Landlady...

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:37.180
Do you really think I can be an actress?

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:42.220
Maybe you can start behind the scenes 
instead of jumping right into acting.

00:14:42.220 --> 00:14:43.190
Behind the scenes?

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:47.440
There's a lot of work to do in a 
theater troupe besides just acting.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:51.720
Like makeup, set design, script writing,

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:54.430
and putting together props and costumes.

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:55.450
Oh...

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:59.150
They also need someone to 
book venues for after-parties,

00:14:59.150 --> 00:15:00.820
and people to prepare meals.

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:02.620
That's the most important thing!

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:04.580
I want to work behind the scenes!

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:07.470
I'm good with my hands, 
and I can make clothes!

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:10.300
No, Mayu-chan, you need 
to be front and center.

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:11.220
Why?

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.860
Because you're as cute as a doll.

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:17.120
She's right. You have a nice
voice, too. It carries well.

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:20.390
Mayu-chan, you'd look great
 in a princess role!

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:23.730
I'm telling you, I can't!

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:28.490
In the first place, we haven't 
even decided we're going to—

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:28.490
I'm up for it.

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:32.240
Hearing them talk about it 
made it sound kinda fun.

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:35.280
I've always been interested in 
things like scripts, anyway.

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:37.120
And above all,

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:39.370
I want to support Hina-chan.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:41.870
Kuu-chan...

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:47.500
Also, I want to see Mayu-chan 
playing a princess.

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:50.630
I told you, I'm not going to be an actress!

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:53.250
I think you'd be a perfect fit, though...

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:55.050
Jeez!

00:15:57.830 --> 00:15:59.740
I'm getting hungry.

00:15:59.740 --> 00:16:02.500
But we just had breakfast...

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:05.150
It's a little early, but shall we have lunch?

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:09.150
<b> The new fabric softener I bought to try out 
the other day smells so nice too... 

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:09.150
<b>The weather's nice today, 
so it's a perfect day to do the laundry!

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:10.650
<b>Today's Opening Time 
12:30 
Please Bear With Us</b>

00:16:09.810 --> 00:16:13.010
But even if we do start a theater troupe,

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:17.200
is there a place where 
we could practice acting?

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:21.320
I was thinking we could make a stage 
at the back of the coffee shop

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:23.290
and use it as a theater.

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:25.730
You've thought that far ahead?

00:16:25.730 --> 00:16:27.790
You're really into this idea, huh?

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:33.920
I always thought it'd be nice if we could 
hold regular stage productions here someday.

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:35.180
If we could do that...

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:38.330
...we'd draw more customers here, too.

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:41.520
You're more shrewd than I thought...

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:45.140
It would conform with the 
apartment rules, so why not?

00:16:45.140 --> 00:16:47.310
Oh, that's right...

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:51.010
Yep! Residents have to work here in the shop!

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:53.100
If you don't want to be in the troupe,

00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:55.200
would you rather work in the coffee shop?

00:16:55.840 --> 00:16:58.810
W-W-W-Wel...

00:16:58.810 --> 00:17:03.330
W-Wel...c-co...

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:06.580
Or would you rather work 
in the used bookstore?

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:15.800
I-I-Is... Is th-this... 
the book you're l-looki—

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:14.840
<b>The Setting Sun</b>

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:19.870
I-I'd like to be in the 
theater troupe, please.

00:17:19.870 --> 00:17:21.000
Then that settles it!

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:22.150
Let's do our best.

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:23.600
Looking forward to it, principal.

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:26.820
A-Actually, about that...

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:30.820
I think you'd make a better principal.

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:33.430
I only jumped on board with your idea.

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:37.490
B-Besides, Aki-chan has to deal 
with her work as landlady, too.

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:41.380
Is working as a landlady really that busy?

00:17:41.380 --> 00:17:42.370
Just accept it!

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:47.730
Me as the principal of the 
troupe... I couldn't...

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:48.850
Don't worry.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:54.560
I don't think anyone wants this theater 
troupe to happen more than you do.

00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:55.630
You can do it.

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:59.390
O... O... O...

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:03.110
Okay! I'll try my best!

00:18:03.110 --> 00:18:06.890
I-I'm inexperienced, but I'll be 
counting on your support!

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.970
We're looking forward to it.

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:13.900
Buy for Tomorrow: 
Coffee Beans 
Filters

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:10.710
Let's work hard, Hina-chan!

00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:12.760
Can't wait, Principal!

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:15.900
<b>Today's Opening Time 
14:00 
Please Bear With Us</b>

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:18.240
If we're going to start a theater troupe,

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:20.470
we'll need to come up with a troupe name.

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:22.010
Anyone have an idea?

00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:25.160
Since it was her idea, it should 
include Hina-chan's name!

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:27.500
Yeah, good idea.

00:18:28.010 --> 00:18:29.670
How about the Hinako Troupe?

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:33.290
Or, for more impact, maybe Hinako Deluxe.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.800
Or maybe Hinako and Her Merry Band?

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:38.690
What do you think, Hina-chan?

00:18:38.690 --> 00:18:43.040
Huh? A-A... A...

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:43.990
A?

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:48.430
The apartment's name, Hitotose...

00:18:48.740 --> 00:18:51.440
So, the Hitotose Troupe?

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:54.940
The Hitotose Troupe... I like it!

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:57.220
The Hitotose Troupe...

00:18:57.220 --> 00:18:58.950
Yeah. I guess it's settled.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:04.580
The Hitotose Troupe.

00:19:04.900 --> 00:19:08.560
Okay! Now that our troupe has a name,

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:10.610
I need to open the shop.

00:19:10.610 --> 00:19:11.590
U-Um...

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:16.880
C-Can I get all of your contact information?

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:18.590
Oh, right.

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:24.130
An SNS might be better than email.

00:19:24.130 --> 00:19:26.820
Which SNS do you use?

00:19:26.820 --> 00:19:28.550
W-Well...

00:19:28.550 --> 00:19:33.090
I'm sorry... what is an SNS?

00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:34.480
We're starting there?!

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:37.260
Now touch here.

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:40.240
That's it! Now press this, and...

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:47.490
Something popped up!

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:49.750
<b>Mom 
Kuina 
Chiaki 
Mayuki</b>

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:53.580
That's all of us. You can contact us anytime.

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:55.380
Thank you!

00:19:58.700 --> 00:20:01.030
Now, then...

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:04.270
I'm going to open the shop, okay?

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:05.510
Huh?

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:09.520
U-Uh... C-Can I have more pasta?

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:10.890
You want to eat more?!

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:15.770
<b>Mom 
Kuina 
Chiaki 
Mayuki</b>

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:23.570
I got all these new contacts in just one day!

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:26.280
<b>Kuina</b>

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:26.280
<b>Are you awake?</b>

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:28.980
Eh... Ah...

00:20:28.980 --> 00:20:30.850
Yes, I'm awake!

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:32.280
Hello?

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:39.840
Kuu-chan, you're here!

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:41.550
The others are here, too.

00:20:42.530 --> 00:20:44.460
Mayu-chan! Miss Landlady!

00:20:44.460 --> 00:20:46.470
Mind if we come in?

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:51.920
U-Um, what brings you all here?

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:55.770
We were wondering if you'd decided 
what we should do with the troupe.

00:20:56.050 --> 00:21:00.780
No, I don't even know 
where we should start...

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:03.630
I guess you don't have 
any stage experience yet.

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:08.590
So we did some research on theater troupes.

00:21:08.590 --> 00:21:13.250
And we found that there's a famous place 
in Shimokitazawa called Suzuran...

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:14.290
It's this.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.290
<b>Theater News</b>

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:21.380
It's a very historical theater that 
everyone dreams of performing in.

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:22.800
Really?

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:23.420
Yep.

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:26.070
Why don't we try to get there?

00:21:26.070 --> 00:21:27.930
To someplace that amazing?

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:31.810
I'm in. It's always better to dream big.

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:35.360
I'm all for it, too. 
Let's work hard together.

00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:37.940
Okay!

00:21:38.850 --> 00:21:41.400
Then Suzuran will be our goal.

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:44.150
Let's put together a great act!

00:21:44.390 --> 00:21:45.030
Yep.

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:46.030
Right!

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:47.360
Yeah!

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:49.680
Leave the script to me!

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:49.680
I can't wait!

00:21:48.770 --> 00:21:49.680
Yeah!

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:53.620
I'm excited.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:35.260
<b>Mistaken Friend</b>

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:28.340
It's always better to dream big!

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:31.590
Bigger taiyaki and dorayaki 
are always more exciting, too!

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:33.220
School's about to start, too.

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:37.620
Just thinking about what awaits 
in our future makes me so excited!

00:23:37.620 --> 00:23:39.930
Next time: "Mistaken Friend."
